1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,075
Terribly cold it was, and almost dark —
the last evening of the year.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,325
A poor little girl shuffled along in her
mother's big slippers.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,080
Two carriages raced by — she lost them,

4
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:18,950
a boy ran off with one, and now she was
barefoot.

5
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,375
Matches… who'll buy my matches?

6
00:00:21,725 --> 00:00:25,300
All day, no one had bought a single match.

7
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:29,975
Candles gleamed in every window, and it
smelled of roast goose.

8
00:00:30,325 --> 00:00:35,775
She huddled in a corner, afraid to go
home: her father would beat her.

9
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:40,450
Her hands were numb. If only she dared
strike one match…

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,075
How it blazed! It was like sitting by a
great, warm iron stove.

11
00:00:46,425 --> 00:00:50,375
Then the flame went out, and the stove was
gone.

12
00:00:50,725 --> 00:00:56,175
She struck another. The wall turned to a
veil; inside, a roast goose steamed.

13
00:00:56,525 --> 00:01:01,225
It hopped down and waddled toward her —
and the match went out.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,075
With the third, she sat beneath a great
Christmas tree, ablaze with candles.

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,700
It went out. The lights rose up and became
stars. One fell.

16
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:14,375
Someone is dying.

17
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,981
Her grandmother, the only one who ever
loved her,

18
00:01:19,981 --> 00:01:24,450
had told her: when a star falls, a soul
goes up to God.

19
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:28,750
One more match — and there stood
Grandmother, shining and kind.

20
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,175
Grandmother! Take me with you!

21
00:01:31,525 --> 00:01:35,850
She struck the whole bundle at once, to
keep her near.

22
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:40,160
Grandmother took her in her arms, and they
flew up,

23
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:44,275
so high — where there is no cold, no
hunger, no fear.

24
00:01:44,625 --> 00:01:47,319
In the cold dawn sat the little girl,

25
00:01:47,319 --> 00:01:50,450
rosy-cheeked and smiling — frozen to
death.

26
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:52,875
She wanted to warm herself.

27
00:01:53,225 --> 00:01:56,700
No one knew the beautiful things she had
seen,

28
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:00,175
or the joy she had found with her
grandmother.

